\pard\plain \ltrch\loch {\f1\fs24\b1 Marcellus Athos}
\par\plain \f1\fs18\b1
\par\plain {\f1\fs18\b1 Ethnicity:}{\f2\fs18\b0  Russian.}
\par\plain {\f1\fs18\b1 Position:}{\f2\fs18\b0  Commander of the Protectant.}
\par\plain {\f1\fs18\b1 Age:}{\f2\fs18\b0  Not stated.}
\par\plain {\f1\fs18\b1 Sex:}{\f2\fs18\b0  Male.}
\par\plain {\f1\fs18\b1 Height:}{\f2\fs18\b0  Not stated.}
\par\plain {\f1\fs18\b1 Build:}{\f2\fs18\b0  Commanding presence.}
\par\plain {\f1\fs18\b1 Role in Story:}{\f2\fs18\b0  Principal human antagonist. Marcellus directs the hidden mission to the lost facility, conceals the truth about the sentients, and later tries to contain or destroy the evidence John uncovers.}
\par\plain {\f1\fs18\b1 Goal:}{\f2\fs18\b0  Maintain centralized control over advanced systems, suppress destabilising truths, and keep humanity's future within the chain of command.}
\par\plain {\f1\fs18\b1 Physical Description:}{\f2\fs18\b0  Formal, imposing and intensely self-styled. Even his bridge doors advertise his authority in bronze calligraphy.}
\par\plain {\f1\fs18\b1 Personality:}{\f2\fs18\b0  Calculating, authoritarian, secretive and deeply paternalistic. He speaks about stability, but his instinct is always control.}
\par\plain {\f1\fs18\b1 Occupation:}{\f2\fs18\b0  Protectant commander and operational arbiter.}
\par\plain {\f1\fs18\b1 Habits/Mannerisms:}{\f2\fs18\b0  Paces bridge decks with his arms behind his back. Leans over terminals during crises. Turns every conversation into a test of loyalty.}
\par\plain {\f1\fs18\b1 Background:}{\f2\fs18\b0  Oversaw the lost-facility narrative, treated the sentients as a threat to be contained, and built a career around command-level management of the CLEAR-era order.}
\par\plain {\f1\fs18\b1 Internal Conflicts:}{\f2\fs18\b0  He seems to believe he is protecting civilisation, but distrust has narrowed his imagination into control at any cost.}
\par\plain {\f1\fs18\b1 External Conflicts:}{\f2\fs18\b0  Opposed by Ava politically, by John ethically, and by Wolfgang's legacy technologically.}
\par\plain {\f1\fs18\b1 Notes:}{\f2\fs18\b0  Marcellus is the clearest embodiment of the novel's warning that even noble systems become dangerous in the hands of people who cannot release power.}
\par\plain \f2\fs18\b0}